## memracer

This session is connected to a memracer MCP server; the user submits work by
talking to you. Follow the `memracer-protocol` skill. In short, without the
user naming any tool:

- **Session start**: call `human_status`; surface tasks by state and any open
  questions (offer to answer them via `human_answer`). Lead with any
  `attention_alerts`: they mean queued work has passed its attention grace
  while no coder has a live lease in that project. Offer the alert's recovery
  action; do not describe it as a crash or data loss.
- **User shares an idea, bug, or complaint**: gather evidence from this repo
  first — file:line references, code snippets, stack traces, `git rev-parse
  HEAD` — infer `owner/name` from `git remote get-url origin`, then call
  `human_submit` with title, body with acceptance criteria, repo, base_sha,
  and the evidence. Report the task id and grooming verdict.
